				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jaymzwww66" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5591853); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5591853&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834554" alt="JaymzWWW66" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5591853)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jaymzwww66" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5591853); return false;" >JaymzWWW66</a></span> <span class="odate time_1569606421 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Sep 2019 17:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4378874">
									

<p>I really enjoyed the read. I liked that you created a skip that allowed for you to write several types of stories while still maintaining a professional write up. I have seen more than a few entries use blue text to show updates to the log, but I believe this is the first time I have seen all these different colors being used. It works very well, is creative, and exceedingly unique among SCP entries.</p>
<p>Some points I think could be worked on:</p>
<ol>
<li>test logs for all the pens</li>
<li>more information for the black pen. The [DATA EXPUNGED] does make sense in context, but perhaps you could have a code that says &quot;Enter 05 credentials&quot; and provide small details.</li>
<li>The interview could be improved a bit. As Damian Uck pointed out, if the pens were pretty simple to make, why not make another set?</li>
</ol>
<p>All in all, a strongly unique entry, with some room to be fleshed out. It's a +1 from me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
